The Rhylthyme MCP tools are unavailable in this offline session, so I cannot run `validate_program`, `analyze_schedule`, or `visualize_schedule`, and therefore cannot return a live URL or Gantt output. I built and manually checked the program against the authoring rules.

Improved question: **“For each timed activity, is it hands-on work that one cook must do exclusively, unattended equipment work that can overlap with other steps, or passive rest/chill/drain work that only has to be complete before serving?”** This exposes hidden timing dependencies such as: the oven must be hot before baking; the batter must rest before cooking; the griddle must heat before pancakes; coffee must be set up before brewing and timed to finish with the pancakes; bacon can be held warm; fruit salad should chill enough but can finish early; and final serving must wait for all hot/cold components to be ready.

The revised plan treats mixing, cutting, squeezing, coffee setup, and serving as `prep` hands-on work; oven baking, griddle heating/cooking, chilling, resting, draining, and brewing as separate resource lines that can overlap where appropriate. Coffee brewing uses a compound trigger tied to the start of pancake cooking plus a 7-minute offset so it ends exactly when the pancakes finish.

